Subject: [PATCH] common_sensor_launch: keep the nUWAy distortion corrector thresholds

The nUWAy sensor kit shipped its own copy of common_sensor_launch, forked from
an older upstream. That copy is dropped in favour of the one in 1.9.0, which is
newer (0.52.0 vs 0.50.0) and whose other differences are upstream refactors
(PathJoinSubstitution instead of eager os.path.join).

The one genuine nUWAy change is carried here: both distortion corrector
thresholds were relaxed from 0.01 to 0.07 on the vehicle. Keeping the validated
values is the safer default.

Revisit once the tighter upstream thresholds are shown to hold on this stack -
if the diagnostics stay quiet at 0.01, drop this patch.
---
--- a/sensor_kit/sample_sensor_kit_launch/common_sensor_launch/config/distortion_corrector_node.param.yaml
+++ b/sensor_kit/sample_sensor_kit_launch/common_sensor_launch/config/distortion_corrector_node.param.yaml
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@
     has_static_tf_only: false
     use_3d_distortion_correction: false
     update_azimuth_and_distance: false
-    processing_time_threshold_sec: 0.01
-    timestamp_mismatch_fraction_threshold: 0.01
+    processing_time_threshold_sec: 0.07
+    timestamp_mismatch_fraction_threshold: 0.07
